cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SolidarityNode, please cite it as below."
title: "SolidarityNode: an open-source spatial probabilistic framework for social service accessibility, latent need, vulnerability and resilience"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "SolidarityNode contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SolidarityNode/snode"
url: "https://solidaritynode.github.io/snode/"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  SolidarityNode estimates accessibility, latent social need, social vulnerability and the
  resilience of social service networks with Bayesian networks, dynamic Bayesian networks,
  Monte Carlo simulation and network analysis, at the level of spatial unit, social group,
  service and time. Early development: version 0.1.0 provides the platform foundation with a
  diagnostic model only, and no research results.
keywords:
  - social services
  - accessibility
  - hidden need
  - vulnerability
  - resilience
  - Bayesian networks
  - spatial analysis
